				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/electrix" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6191880); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6191880&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606942354" alt="Electrix" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6191880)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/electrix" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6191880); return false;" >Electrix</a></span> <span class="odate time_1604775425 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">07 Nov 2020 18:57</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4813285">
									

<p>First of all:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Open&nbsp;Crit;&nbsp;Story</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Close&nbsp;Crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>As far as I can tell, there is no story. Sure, there is some background and the exploration log has some progression, but there is nothing that actually says why it exists. If you're writing an SCP nowadays, one of the most important things is that it has a good backstory and motivation: Why does it do what it does? Where does it come from? In all earnesty, there is a big chance this isn't going to get accepted onto the site if you don't figure this out. The idea is cool, yes, but it lacks depth. The era's of the ''Thing that does a thing'' SCP's are long gone.</p>
<p>I've looked at the crits of some other people here, and they're saying the same thing. I hate to say it to you, but i'm going to advise that you do a complete or partial re-write. So:</p>
<ol>
<li>Discuss your idea with other people on the platform; make sure it has depth but isn't too complex or convoluted (more experienced writers can give some good advise on this topic)</li>
<li>Rewrite your story with the new idea in mind and pay attention to crit people are giving you</li>
</ol>
<p>If you want some help with this, go read some guides in the guide hub (see the sidebar @ guides and essays, and go read some guides under ''Guides for writing'') You could also create a post on the ideas critique forum or reach out to people in IRC about your idea.</p>
<p>Also, before I jump into the errors I've picked out, not_a_seagull's recommendations are pretty good and should probs. be followed.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>The following are a couple of tips on what can be improved per section (These are meant as general tips so you don't make the same mistakes again):</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Open&nbsp;Crit;&nbsp;Containment&nbsp;procedures</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Close&nbsp;Crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>First of all: Get rid of all the small, two to three sentence long paragraphs and combine them into 1 or 2 longer paragraphs that detail containment procedures. It makes it easier to read and looks nicer! Also, I would leave the last paragraph out, as it doesn't really make sense; why are only 55% of Tremor Events censored? Isn't it better to contain all information? Earthquakes don't just appear out of nowhere after all. This is especially true if SCP-XXXX manifests in a portion of the world where earthquakes don't appear. There's also a couple of structuring, grammar and tone errors:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>All instances of SCP-XXXX-2 after an event are to be plucked and incinerated unless required for research.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>''<strong>After an event, all instances of SCP-XXXX-2</strong> are to be plucked and incinerated unless required for research.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Any reports of dangerous tremors within the world, the Foundation is to interrogate and amnestize survivors that witnessed SCP-XXXX during the event.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>''<strong>After</strong> any reports of dangerous tremors within the world, the Foundation <strong>is</strong> (or <strong>Foundation field agents are</strong>) to interrogate and amnestize survivors that witnessed SCP-XXXX during the event.''</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Once the Hostile Trembler Event is fully completed, all survivors are to be amnesticized.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>''Once the Hostile Trembler Event <strong>concludes</strong>, all survivors are to be amnesticized.''</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Open&nbsp;Crit;&nbsp;Description</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Close&nbsp;Crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>In a description, you need to describe everything. This includes SCP-XXXX-2, which is currently missing. Also, SCP-XXXX should probs be changed to SCP-XXXX-1. It could probs. be shortened, but if you're willing to keep everything:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Witnesses of a Trembler Events describe SCP-XXXX to be an adolescent male wearing a black hoodie, and camouflage cargo pants, spray-painted with various luminescent colors.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;Witnesses of a Trembler Events describe SCP-XXXX to be an adolescent male wearing a black hoodie<strong><span style="text-decoration: line-through;">,</span></strong> and camouflage cargo pants, <strong>the latter</strong> spray-painted with various luminescent colors.&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>It is currently impossible to view SCP-XXXX's facial features, as the shadow of the hood covers it.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>''It is currently impossible to view SCP-XXXX's facial features, as <strong>it's obscured by its hood</strong>.&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>However, a soft aqua glow in the shape of a smiley face pierces the shadow.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>''However, a soft <strong>aquamarine</strong> glow in the shape of a smiley face <strong>is present where its facial features would otherwise be</strong>.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>A string hangs off SCP-XXXX side that carries four different illuminated colored spray-cans.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>''A string hangs off <strong>SCP-XXXX's</strong> side <strong>that's attatched to</strong> four <strong>luminescent</strong> spray-cans.&quot;&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The stereo appears to have no tape within it but still manages to generate audio through anomalous means.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>''The stereo appears to have no tape <strong>inside of</strong> it but still manages to generate audio <strong>by</strong> anomalous means.''</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Though the nature of its anomalous properties remains mostly uncertain, SCP-XXXX appears fully capable of instantaneous travel to any location on earth. This causes standard containment impossible.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>''Though the nature of its anomalous properties remains mostly uncertain, SCP-XXXX appears <strong>to be</strong> <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">fully</span> capable of instantaneous travel to any location on earth. This causes standard containment <strong>to be</strong> impossible. (this should be refrenced in the special containment procedures)''</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-XXXX wasn't discovered by the Foundation until 2003. Witnesses report its arrival during a Trembler Event. MTF Epsilon-43 (&quot;Pink Eye&quot;) investigated the aftermath, and spotted SCP-XXXX sap from an SCP-XXXX-2 instance with a modified glass syringe, on the east side of the town. SCP-XXXX instantaneously dematerialized from the scene when it observed the unit.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>''SCP-XXXX <strong>was</strong> discovered by the Foundation <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">until</span> <strong>in</strong> 2003. Witnesses <strong>reported</strong> its arrival during a Trembler Event. MTF Epsilon-43 (&quot;Pink Eye&quot;) investigated the aftermath <span style="text-decoration: line-through;"><strong>,</strong></span> and spotted SCP-XXXX sap (you need to give this a name; SCP-XXXX-2-A perhaps?) from an SCP-XXXX-2 instance <strong>in</strong> a modified glass syringe, on the east side of the town (in which town exactly? Specify the location). SCP-XXXX instantaneously dematerialized <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">from the scene</span> when it observed the unit.''<br />
(It's handy for this to be put in a seperate addendum named ''Discovery'')</p>
<blockquote>
<p>In all known Trembler Events, the affected areas have had a population over 600. In addition, all events occur at 0000 hours local time.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>''In all known Trembler Events, the affected areas <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">have</span> had a population <strong>of</strong> over 600 <strong>residents</strong>. In addition, all events occur at 00<strong>:</strong>00 hours local time.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Oddly, SCP-XXXX is capable of playing audio that has not released at that year. The audio would release on a later date through conventional means.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>''Oddly, SCP-XXXX is capable of playing <strong>music</strong> that has not released <strong>yet</strong>. The <strong>music</strong> would release on a later date through conventional means.''</p>
<blockquote>
<p>A trembler event procedes as follows:</p>
</blockquote>
<p>In the way you've written it, I would suggest you convert it into a collapsible block, and seperate all steps of the Trembler Event into different lines. This makes it way easier to read.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The subject reaches into its pocket to reveal its modified glass syringe filled with SCP-XXXX-2 sap.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>''<strong>SCP-XXXX</strong> reaches into its pocket to reveal <strong>a</strong> modified glass syringe filled with SCP-XXXX-2 sap (SCP-XXXX-2-A, or whatever you want to call it. Just come up with a tag for it).''</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The entity then inject its median cubital and return the syringe.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>''The entity then inject its median cubital and <strong>puts</strong> the syringe <strong>in its pocket</strong>.''</p>
<blockquote>
<p>If uninterrupted, SCP-XXXX will stop its music and exhale spores of SCP-XXXX-2 instances.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>''If uninterrupted, SCP-XXXX will stop its music and exhale spores of SCP-XXXX-2 instances <strong>at the end of the Trembler Event</strong>''</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Interruption either through deactivation of its portable stereo or a halt in its movement.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>''<strong>It's interrupted</strong> either through deactivation of its portable stereo or a halt in its movement.&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>100% of Trembler Events destroy a large portion of the targetted area and causes a high number of deaths.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>''<strong>All Hostile</strong> Trebler Events destroy a large portion of the targetted area and causes a high number of deaths.''</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Open&nbsp;Crit;&nbsp;Addenda</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Close&nbsp;Crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<ol>
<li>The experiment log is pretty good, if unessicary. You could just implement it into your description.</li>
<li>The interview is uneccisary. It's just filler and there for no reason. If you're willing, writing something else in its place. Otherwise, just delete it.</li>
<li>Oh god the writing is all over the place! If you're going to write an exploration log like that, DO IT WITH TIMESTAMPS AND MAKE IT INTO A LOG! I cannot stress enough how this would improve your draft. If it's just a description of the exploration, than you need to remove everything that has something to do with how the characters feel, like ''Gasps audibly'' or ''Is annoyed by&#8230;''. For how you've written it, you should convert it into an exploration log. An article that does this excellently is <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2935">SCP-2935</a>, so go give it a read if you want some inspiration!</li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Hopefully it's helpfull!</p>
<p>(Asked to look at this through SkipIRC)</p>

