		<div class="post" id="post-4801213">
		<div class="long">
			<div class="head">
									<div class="options">
						<a href="javascript:;" onclick="togglePostFold(event,4801213)" class="btn btn-default btn-small btn-sm">Fold</a>
					</div>
								<div class="title" id="post-title-4801213">
																		Re: SCP draft Crit
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/not-a-seagull" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3009022); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3009022&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606942354" alt="not_a_seagull" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3009022)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/not-a-seagull" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3009022); return false;" >not_a_seagull</a></span> <span class="odate time_1603320419 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">21 Oct 2020 22:46</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4801213">
									

<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;SPaG,&nbsp;Logic,&nbsp;and&nbsp;Tone</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>You probably shouldn't have both ACS and the standard header at the same time.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>If SCP-XXXX Event has been identified</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;If <strong>an</strong> SCP-XXXX Event has been identified&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>the nearest MTF unit is to dispatch to SCP-XXXX current location immediately</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;the nearest MTF unit <strong>must</strong> dispatch to SCP-XXXX<strong>'s</strong> current location&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>They are then tasked to follow it and apprehend any individuals that attempt to interrupt SCP-XXXX active phase.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;They <strong>should</strong> follow it and apprehend any individuals that attempt to interrupt SCP-XXXX<strong>'s</strong> active phase.&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>If SCP-XXXX does get interrupted, causing a Hostile SCP-XXXX Event,</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;If SCP-XXXX <strong>is</strong> interrupted,&quot; Axe the last part.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>any survivors that witnessed SCP-XXXX are to be amnesticized.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Axe &quot;that witnessed&quot;. If they survived SCP-XXXX it's implied that they witnessed it.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>without the Foundations knowledge</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Foundation<strong>'</strong>s</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Any reports of a &quot;natural disaster&quot; anywhere within world</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;<strong>After a</strong>ny reports of a &quot;natural disaster&quot; anywhere within world&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>is to interview and amnesticized any individual</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;is to interview and <strong>amnesticize</strong> any individual&quot;, although the wording &quot;is to interrogate and give amnestics to any individual&quot; is cleaner.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Witnesses of an SCP-XXXX Events describe SCP-XXXX to be an adolescent male wearing a black hoodie, spray-painted various colors that illuminate and black cargo pants.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;Witnesses of an SCP-XXXX Events describe SCP-XXXX to be an adolescent male wearing a black hoodie, spray-painted <strong>with</strong> various <strong>neon</strong> colors<strong>,</strong> and black cargo pants&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>It is currently impossible to view SCP-XXXX facial features</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;It is currently impossible to view SCP-XXXX's facial features&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The only light penetrating through is that of an illuminate aqua spray-paint that resembles a smiley face.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'd say &quot;However, a soft aqua glow in the shape of a smiley face pierces the shadow.&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-XXXX has consistently been seen wearing on-ear headphones and carries a spray-painted Victrola VBB-10-SLV model portable stereo.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The tense here changes mid sentence. I'd say &quot;SCP-XXXX carries headphones and a spray-painted Victrola VBB-10-SLV model portable stereo.&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Though the nature of its anomalous properties remains mostly uncertain, SCP-XXXX appears fully capable of instantaneous travel to any location on earth. Effectively nullifying containment.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Sentence fragment. Try &quot;This makes standard containment impossible&quot; instead.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-XXXX active phase occur completely random in any populated area</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;SCP-XXXX<strong>'s</strong> active phase <strong>may</strong> occur in any populated area&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The process to fully complete an SCP-XXXX Event ranges from one to nine hours.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Instead of &quot;process&quot;, I'd say &quot;time required&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>In all known SCP-XXXX Events, the affected areas have shared the following characteristics of an area with a population over 300, and all events occur on 12:00 PM precisely.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'd split this into two sentences, and say:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>In all known SCP-XXXX Events, the affected areas have had a population over 300. In addition, all events occur <strong>at 1200 hours local time</strong>.</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>An SCP-XXXX Event proceeds as follow:</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;An SCP-XXXX Event proceeds as follow<strong>s</strong>:&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-XXXX will instantaneously travel</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Instead of &quot;instantaneously travel&quot;, I'd say &quot;manifest&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>around the streets/pathways of the area aimlessly</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'd axe &quot;of the area&quot; and say &quot;local streets/pathways&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-XXXX will have been playing music from its portable stereo loudly and act out a hip-hop style dance that varies in several actions, throughout its wandering.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'd rearrange this sentence to say: &quot;While wandering, SCP-XXXX will play music from its portable stereo and preform a hip-hop dance.&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-XXXX will continue this wandering phase, ranging from one hour to nine hours</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;SCP-XXXX will continue wandering <strong>for the next</strong> one to nine hours&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>it will cause a Hostile SCP-XXXX Event</p>
</blockquote>
<p>cause =&gt; begin</p>
<blockquote>
<p>All that is known of SCP-XXXX is a few anomalous properties here and there.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This doesn't sound formal. I'd say &quot;All we know about SCP-XXXX are the disastrous consequences of interfering with it.&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>However, it has been discovered that there is no such thing as a natural disaster, at least not the way society studies and portrays it. Natural disasters were believed to be the earth's way of showing pollution or destruction from humanity.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'll talk about this more later. However, what does it <em>mean</em> that the Earth is retaliating against humanity for pollution? Tornados, hurricanes and earthquakes have been happening even before humanity appeared.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>except for a few folklore stories</p>
</blockquote>
<p>These &quot;folklore stories&quot; are only mentioned here, but not in the recovery?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>If any individual reading this document doesn't have level 5 access entry, are cleared for immediate termination.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I don't see why knowing that natural disasters aren't actually &quot;natural&quot; would mean that one should be killed immediately.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Structure&nbsp;and&nbsp;Narrative</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>This SCP is a pretty long setup for a pretty medicore plot twist at the end. We find out there's a guy that plays music, in a Description that could probably be shortened significantly without losing much information. Then we read about some Events, a part which isn't really necessary. Finally, we read the Discovery, then that Discovery is immediately torn down with a plot twist that doesn't make much sense.</p>
<p>If SCP-XXXX has really been causing all of these natural disasters, why hasn't it been noticed until 2011? Also, what's SCP-XXXX doing on the ocean, since that's where all of these hurricanes start?</p>
<p>In addition, SCP-XXXX feels like an empty vessel. &quot;Apathy&quot; towards the human race is mentioned towards the end, but this apathy is told to the reader, rather than shown to the reader.</p>
<p>If I were you, I'd replace the log of SCP-XXXX Events with an interview log with SCP-XXXX or two. Putting a personality of some kind into SCP-XXXX would add some value to the SCP and make it a more engaging read. Maybe have it explain why it produces natural disasters, and why it chooses hiphop of all things.</p>
<p>Then, I'd replace the note at the end with an incident log. I would do something related to the interview logs to help flesh out SCP-XXXX just a little more. Maybe MTF Theta-23 (&quot;Dancing Queens&quot;) challenges SCP-XXXX to a rap battle, if I may suggest something goofy. Alternatively, maybe it talks with another one of its kind?</p>
<p>In any case, giving SCP-XXXX a little more depth would go a long way for this draft.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Once you've revised, feel free to DM me and I'll give another look.</p>

							</div>

								
