																		Re: SCP draft Crit
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/barbarous-bread" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6880816); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6880816&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606942354" alt="Barbarous Bread" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6880816)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/barbarous-bread" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6880816); return false;" >Barbarous Bread</a></span> <span class="odate time_1603371154 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">22 Oct 2020 12:52</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4801575">
									

<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;close</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Based on the article header, the article itself is Level 5 classified, but at the bottom you have a section that you need Level 5 credentials to access. If you already accessed the article with those same credentials, then that becomes redundant. So either lower the access to the article itself or have a different title for the last collapsible.</p>
<hr />
<blockquote>
<p>&#8230; are to be monitored between 10:00 PM until 9:00 AM for any reports of loud music playing at 12:00 PM in high populated locations.</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>all events occur at 1200 hours local time.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I feel like it would be in the best interest to use 24hr time for any time notations in your article. As well, the first part doesn't align to when you say the events occur. You say the channels are monitored at night when the events occur at noon (00:00 is midnight in 24hr time).</p>
<hr />
<blockquote>
<p>the nearest MTF unit <strong>imust</strong> dispatch to SCP-XXXX's current location</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Britanny</strong>: Where am I? Who are you, people? You have something to do [<strong>with</strong>] this, don't you!</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Typos.</p>
<hr />
<blockquote>
<p>The MTF unit reported this in, and the Foundation was on the search for SCP-XXXX</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Awkward phrasing.</p>
<p>e.g. &quot;Based on the MTF report, the Foundation began searching for SCP-XXXX.&quot;</p>
<hr />
<p>There are some sections that are pretty awkward and either lack some details and/or also provides extraneous details.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>On 12/08/1984, an instance of SCP-XXXX-C occurred in Florida, United States that caused severe damage to the local area. Surprisingly, the individual that interrupted SCP-XXXX active phase survived the disaster. Her name was Britanny McGlockly, she was recovered unconscious lying on the concrete with rubble on her arms and legs. She was taken to a hospital immediately when recovered. Two Foundation agents were sent to interview her to describe the event from her perspective. <em>(See interview log)</em></p>
</blockquote>
<p>e.g.</p>
<hr />
<blockquote>
<p>In every natural disaster event since the discovery, SCP-XXXX has been involved. From 1984 to 2020. Leading researchers to believe this overall theory that SCP-XXXX causes natural disasters to occur.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>e.g.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>In every natural disaster event since it's discovery in 1984, SCP-XXXX has had some involvement. This has lead researchers to believe that SCP-XXXX causes &quot;natural disasters&quot; to occur.</p>
</blockquote>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>And as a note, I think it's reaching a bit much to say that this SCP is responsible for <em>every</em> natural disaster. Does that include all of them prior to 1984? Every hurricane, tornado, earthquake, drought, etc.?</p>

							</div>

								
					
