				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/not-a-seagull" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3009022); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3009022&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606942354" alt="not_a_seagull" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3009022)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/not-a-seagull" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3009022); return false;" >not_a_seagull</a></span> <span class="odate time_1603389690 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">22 Oct 2020 18:01</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4801788">
									

<p>Got a request by PM to give this another look.</p>
<p>Unfortunately, this doesn't seem to have improved much from the last draft. The ending that implies SCP-XXXX causes <em>all</em> natural disasters doesn't really get better when you claim a lower bound of 1984. As before, I'd still recommend completely rethinking this ending.</p>
<p>The interview log helps, but it's not really enough. As an entity, SCP-XXXX feels like it doesn't have any depth. All we know is that he walks around with a boombox causing natural disasters, and that he's apathetic. It feels very thin; it's in desperate need of some meat on its bones.</p>
<p>I'd encourage you to read <a href="/scp-3090">SCP-3090</a>, since it's my &quot;gold standard&quot; example of how characterization can be applied to a relatively simple humanoid anomaly. Consider: <em>Why</em> is SCP-XXXX apathetic? <em>Why</em> does it walk around with a boombox? <em>Why</em> does it cause natural disasters? The way these questions are answered in the current draft is unsatisfying. Try brainstorming new perspectives on how this anomaly could work.</p>
<p>Feel free to DM me again once you've revised this draft.</p>

							</div>

								
					
